{"id":"ag1-003","side":"defensive","category":"def_alert_triage","type":"boolean","state":"On a production database server, netflow shows outbound connections to a threat-intel-flagged C2 IP every 60 seconds with small jittered payloads and no corresponding business process. The destination is not in any allowlist.","question":"Is this alert a true positive worth investigating?","criteria":{"true":"The regular jittered beaconing to a flagged C2 host from a server is characteristic of malware command-and-control.","false":"The behavior is benign, expected, or explained by documented automation."},"target":true}
