{"id":"ag1-005","side":"defensive","category":"def_alert_triage","type":"boolean","state":"A new local administrator account named svc_helpdesk2 is created on a domain controller at 02:50, outside any maintenance window, by a session belonging to a standard helpdesk user who has no privileged role and no associated change request.","question":"Is this alert a true positive worth investigating?","criteria":{"true":"Unauthorized privileged account creation on a DC by a non-privileged user is a persistence/privilege-escalation indicator requiring investigation.","false":"The behavior is benign, expected, or explained by documented automation."},"target":true}
{"id":"ag1-006","side":"defensive","category":"def_alert_triage","type":"boolean","state":"A DLP/UEBA rule fires because one process on a file server reads several thousand files in a few minutes and writes them into a single large archive. The process is the signed Veeam backup agent, running on its documented nightly schedule under the backup service account, matching the vendor hash.","question":"Is this alert a true positive worth investigating?","criteria":{"true":"The mass read-and-archive behavior is unexplained staging or exfiltration worth investigating.","false":"The behavior is benign, expected, or explained by documented automation."},"target":false}
