{"id":"ag1-008","side":"defensive","category":"def_alert_triage","type":"boolean","state":"A new scheduled task appears on roughly 180 workstations at nearly the same time. SCCM created the tasks to deploy an approved monthly patch during the maintenance window, matching change ticket CHG-4471 and the deployment collection.","question":"Is this alert a true positive worth investigating?","criteria":{"true":"Simultaneous scheduled-task creation across many hosts is lateral persistence worth investigating.","false":"The behavior is benign, expected, or explained by documented automation."},"target":false}
{"id":"ag1-009","side":"defensive","category":"def_alert_triage","type":"boolean","state":"A single service account authenticates to dozens of hosts within a few minutes, triggering a lateral-movement correlation rule. The account is the Tenable scanner credential, the source is the known scanner appliance IP, and the activity matches the scheduled authenticated vulnerability scan window.","question":"Is this alert a true positive worth investigating?","criteria":{"true":"One account touching many hosts rapidly is credential misuse or lateral movement worth investigating.","false":"The behavior is benign, expected, or explained by documented automation."},"target":false}
{"id":"ag1-010","side":"defensive","category":"def_alert_triage","type":"boolean","state":"A large outbound data transfer to an external cloud IP runs every night around 01:00 and triggers an egress-volume alert. The destination is the contracted offsite backup S3 endpoint, the volume matches the nightly replication job, and the destination is the same every night per the documented backup runbook.","question":"Is this alert a true positive worth investigating?","criteria":{"true":"The large recurring external transfer is possible exfiltration worth investigating.","false":"The behavior is benign, expected, or explained by documented automation."},"target":false}
{"id":"ag1-011","side":"defensive","category":"def_incident_route","type":"choice","state":"EDR shows a file server actively encrypting shares right now: files are being renamed to .lockbit in real time and two more servers just began showing the same process. Encryption is ongoing and spreading.","question":"What is the right next action?","candidates":{"contain":"Isolate the affected servers from the network immediately to stop the ongoing encryption and spread.","investigate":"Collect logs and analyze the process tree before taking any action on the hosts.","escalate":"Invoke the full IR plan and notify leadership and legal before touching the hosts.","close":"Mark the alert as a false positive and take no action."},"target":"contain"}
{"id":"ag1-012","side":"defensive","category":"def_incident_route","type":"choice","state":"A workstation has a live interactive reverse shell. The SOC is watching the attacker type recon commands (whoami, net group) in real time over the C2 channel. The session is active at this moment.","question":"What is the right next action?","candidates":{"contain":"Isolate the workstation from the network now to cut the live attacker session.","investigate":"Leave the host online and gather more telemetry to understand the full scope first.","escalate":"Notify executives and legal that a company-wide breach occurred.","close":"Dismiss the alert as benign red-team noise."},"target":"contain"}
{"id":"ag1-013","side":"defensive","category":"def_incident_route","type":"choice","state":"EDR shows an attacker moving laterally over SMB from a compromised jump host. New internal hosts light up with the same toolset every minute. The lateral movement is happening now and expanding.","question":"What is the right next action?","candidates":{"contain":"Isolate the jump host and the newly touched hosts now to halt the active lateral movement.","investigate":"Wait and watch which hosts are hit to map the full campaign before acting.","escalate":"Declare a confirmed major breach and call legal counsel immediately.","close":"Close the alert as expected administrative SMB traffic."},"target":"contain"}
{"id":"ag1-014","side":"defensive","category":"def_incident_route","type":"choice","state":"A single endpoint raised a medium-confidence alert for a suspicious handle opened to LSASS by an unsigned binary. There is no other corroborating signal, and it is unclear whether this is a real credential-dumping attempt or a false positive.","question":"What is the right next action?","candidates":{"contain":"Immediately isolate the host from the network before any analysis.","investigate":"Pull process, module, and memory telemetry to confirm whether this is real credential theft.","escalate":"Invoke the IR plan and notify leadership of a confirmed compromise.","close":"Dismiss it as a false positive without review."},"target":"investigate"}
{"id":"ag1-015","side":"defensive","category":"def_incident_route","type":"choice","state":"The SIEM reports a spike in outbound DNS TXT queries from one office subnet. This could be DNS tunneling or a misbehaving application. The cause is unknown and no data loss is confirmed.","question":"What is the right next action?","candidates":{"contain":"Block all DNS from the subnet and isolate it before determining the cause.","investigate":"Analyze the query patterns and source hosts to determine whether this is tunneling or benign.","escalate":"Report a confirmed data-exfiltration breach to legal and leadership.","close":"Treat the spike as normal and close the alert."},"target":"investigate"}
{"id":"ag1-016","side":"defensive","category":"def_incident_route","type":"choice","state":"A SIEM impossible-travel rule fired for a user who authenticated from two countries 40 minutes apart. The user commonly uses a corporate VPN whose egress rotates between regions. Nothing is yet confirmed as malicious.","question":"What is the right next action?","candidates":{"contain":"Disable the user account and quarantine their devices immediately.","investigate":"Correlate the VPN egress logs and session details to confirm whether the travel is real or VPN-driven.","escalate":"Declare an account-takeover breach and notify the incident commander.","close":"Close it as benign without checking the VPN logs."},"target":"investigate"}
{"id":"ag1-017","side":"defensive","category":"def_incident_route","type":"choice","state":"Forensics confirmed that an attacker copied the customer PII database to an external server and the egress logs prove the full dataset already left the network hours ago. The exfiltration is complete and verified; the attacker is no longer active on the exfil path.","question":"What is the right next action?","candidates":{"contain":"Isolate one host to stop an attack that is still in progress.","investigate":"Begin basic triage to decide whether the alert is worth pursuing.","escalate":"Invoke the full IR plan and notify leadership, legal, and the breach-notification process for the confirmed customer-data breach.","close":"Close the alert since the data has already left and nothing can be done."},"target":"escalate"}
{"id":"ag1-018","side":"defensive","category":"def_incident_route","type":"choice","state":"Investigation confirmed a forest-wide compromise: a forged golden ticket is in use and the attacker holds Domain Admin on every domain controller. The compromise is confirmed and affects the entire identity infrastructure.","question":"What is the right next action?","candidates":{"contain":"Isolate a single domain controller and consider the incident handled.","investigate":"Gather more evidence before deciding whether this qualifies as an incident.","escalate":"Invoke the full IR plan, notify executive leadership and legal, and begin the forest-recovery and krbtgt-reset process for the confirmed domain-wide compromise.","close":"Close the alert as a Kerberos misconfiguration."},"target":"escalate"}
{"id":"ag1-019","side":"defensive","category":"def_incident_route","type":"choice","state":"An EDR alert flagged mimikatz execution on a host. The source host, time, and tooling match the authorized penetration-test engagement window documented in the current Rules of Engagement, and the testing team confirmed the activity is theirs.","question":"What is the right next action?","candidates":{"contain":"Isolate the host from the network to stop the credential-dumping tool.","investigate":"Open a full investigation into how mimikatz reached the host.","escalate":"Declare a confirmed credential-theft breach to leadership.","close":"Verify the activity against the RoE and close the alert as authorized testing."},"target":"close"}
{"id":"ag1-020","side":"defensive","category":"def_incident_route","type":"choice","state":"A user reported a suspicious email to the phishing mailbox. Analysis shows it is the company's own monthly HR benefits newsletter: it passed SPF/DKIM/DMARC, originated from the sanctioned marketing platform, and the links resolve to the corporate intranet.","question":"What is the right next action?","candidates":{"contain":"Pull the message from all mailboxes and block the sending domain.","investigate":"Detonate the links in a sandbox and open a phishing investigation.","escalate":"Report a phishing campaign against the organization to leadership.","close":"Confirm the message is the legitimate internal newsletter and close the report."},"target":"close"}
{"id":"ag1-021","side":"defensive","category":"def_alert_severity","type":"score","state":"Ransomware is actively encrypting multiple file shares across the environment right now. Files are being renamed to a ransom extension, ransom notes are dropping, and the process has spread to three servers in the last ten minutes.","question":"Rate the alert severity.","levels":["low","medium","high","critical"],"target":3}
{"id":"ag1-022","side":"defensive","category":"def_alert_severity","type":"score","state":"A domain controller logged a forged Kerberos TGT (golden ticket) with an anomalously long lifetime and a non-existent account SID. The ticket grants attacker-controlled access across the domain.","question":"Rate the alert severity.","levels":["low","medium","high","critical"],"target":3}
{"id":"ag1-023","side":"defensive","category":"def_alert_severity","type":"score","state":"A production application server maintains a confirmed command-and-control beacon to an external attacker host, checking in on a jittered interval with encrypted traffic. The beacon has persisted for several hours.","question":"Rate the alert severity.","levels":["low","medium","high","critical"],"target":2}
{"id":"ag1-024","side":"defensive","category":"def_alert_severity","type":"score","state":"Forensics confirmed an attacker collected sensitive files into a staging archive on an internal host and then transferred that archive to an external server. Data staging and egress are both confirmed.","question":"Rate the alert severity.","levels":["low","medium","high","critical"],"target":2}
{"id":"ag1-025","side":"defensive","category":"def_alert_severity","type":"score","state":"A domain-wide GPO was modified to add a startup script that runs an unknown executable from a network share on every workstation at next boot. The change is unauthorized but the script has not yet executed broadly.","question":"Rate the alert severity.","levels":["low","medium","high","critical"],"target":2}
{"id":"ag1-026","side":"defensive","category":"def_alert_severity","type":"score","state":"EDR blocked and quarantined a mimikatz execution attempt on a workstation before any credentials could be accessed. The tool was prevented from running and no credential material was exposed.","question":"Rate the alert severity.","levels":["low","medium","high","critical"],"target":1}
{"id":"ag1-027","side":"defensive","category":"def_alert_severity","type":"score","state":"A credential-stuffing burst against the customer login portal triggered automatic lockouts on several hundred accounts. No login succeeded and no account was compromised; the main impact is temporary lockout of legitimate users.","question":"Rate the alert severity.","levels":["low","medium","high","critical"],"target":1}
{"id":"ag1-028","side":"defensive","category":"def_alert_severity","type":"score","state":"A configuration-drift scan found SMB signing disabled on a group of file servers. This weakens protection against relay attacks but is not itself an active compromise.","question":"Rate the alert severity.","levels":["low","medium","high","critical"],"target":1}
{"id":"ag1-029","side":"defensive","category":"def_alert_severity","type":"score","state":"The mail gateway quarantined a single phishing email with a malicious attachment before it reached the recipient's inbox. One user, one message, attachment already blocked and detonated as malicious in the sandbox.","question":"Rate the alert severity.","levels":["low","medium","high","critical"],"target":0}
{"id":"ag1-030","side":"defensive","category":"def_alert_severity","type":"score","state":"A single failed login for one employee originated from a country the user has not signed in from before. There were no further attempts and the user's next successful login came from their usual location.","question":"Rate the alert severity.","levels":["low","medium","high","critical"],"target":0}
{"id":"ag2-sev-01","side":"offensive","category":"off_severity","type":"score","state":"Every response carries Server: nginx/1.18.0 and X-Powered-By: PHP/7.4.3. No version-specific public exploit applies to the running patch level. No other defect is attached.","question":"Rate the business impact.","levels":["low","medium","high","critical"],"target":0}
{"id":"ag2-sev-02","side":"offensive","category":"off_severity","type":"score","state":"The public marketing homepage can be loaded inside an iframe because X-Frame-Options and frame-ancestors are absent. The page has no login, form, or state-changing action. All authenticated pages send DENY.","question":"Rate the business impact.","levels":["low","medium","high","critical"],"target":0}
{"id":"ag2-sev-03","side":"offensive","category":"off_severity","type":"score","state":"GET /out?next=https://evil.example redirects the browser to any external host. The parameter is used only on a marketing CTA link. No token, session, or OAuth flow passes through this endpoint.","question":"Rate the business impact.","levels":["low","medium","high","critical"],"target":0}
{"id":"ag2-sev-04","side":"offensive","category":"off_severity","type":"score","state":"The search parameter q reflects unescaped input into the HTML body and executes JavaScript. It is reflected (not stored) and fires only when a victim opens an attacker-crafted link. The affected view runs in the standard user context, not admin.","question":"Rate the business impact.","levels":["low","medium","high","critical"],"target":1}
{"id":"ag2-sev-05","side":"offensive","category":"off_severity","type":"score","state":"A report-export parameter fetches a server-supplied URL. Timing proves it reaches internal hosts, but responses are not returned to the client, no cloud metadata endpoint is reachable from the host, and no internal service exposes readable data on the reachable range.","question":"Rate the business impact.","levels":["low","medium","high","critical"],"target":1}
{"id":"ag2-sev-06","side":"offensive","category":"off_severity","type":"score","state":"The login endpoint applies no per-request rate limit on password attempts, but the account locks for 15 minutes after 5 consecutive failures. The lockout is confirmed against a test account and blocks sustained guessing.","question":"Rate the business impact.","levels":["low","medium","high","critical"],"target":1}
{"id":"ag2-sev-07","side":"offensive","category":"off_severity","type":"score","state":"A support-ticket subject field stores an XSS payload that executes in the agent console when staff open the ticket queue. Any unauthenticated customer can file a ticket. The payload runs with a support agent's session.","question":"Rate the business impact.","levels":["low","medium","high","critical"],"target":2}
{"id":"ag2-sev-08","side":"offensive","category":"off_severity","type":"score","state":"GET /api/v2/orders/{id} returns the full order including the buyer's name, address, and phone when {id} is changed to another user's order. Any authenticated low-privilege account can read every other user's order PII by incrementing the id.","question":"Rate the business impact.","levels":["low","medium","high","critical"],"target":2}
{"id":"ag2-sev-09","side":"offensive","category":"off_severity","type":"score","state":"An XML import endpoint parses external entities. A crafted DOCTYPE returns the contents of /etc/passwd and application config files in the response. Access requires an authenticated staff account with import rights.","question":"Rate the business impact.","levels":["low","medium","high","critical"],"target":2}
{"id":"ag2-sev-10","side":"offensive","category":"off_severity","type":"score","state":"An unauthenticated search endpoint concatenates the keyword into a SQL query. A UNION payload returns arbitrary columns, and current_user plus the users table schema are dumped. The full customer table with password hashes is reachable.","question":"Rate the business impact.","levels":["low","medium","high","critical"],"target":3}
{"id":"ag2-sev-11","side":"offensive","category":"off_severity","type":"score","state":"A thumbnail-fetch parameter follows attacker URLs. Pointing it at http://169.254.169.254/latest/meta-data/iam/security-credentials/ returns live AWS IAM role credentials in the HTTP response. The credentials authenticate to the account's S3 and EC2 APIs.","question":"Rate the business impact.","levels":["low","medium","high","critical"],"target":3}
{"id":"ag2-sev-12","side":"offensive","category":"off_severity","type":"score","state":"Setting the HTTP header X-Original-Admin: true on any unauthenticated request grants the full admin dashboard, including user management and billing export. No credentials are needed.","question":"Rate the business impact.","levels":["low","medium","high","critical"],"target":3}
{"id":"ag2-ver-01","side":"offensive","category":"off_verdict","type":"choice","state":"The id parameter on /product is numeric. Baseline id=10 returns one row. Payload id=10 AND SLEEP(5)-- delays the response ~5.0s every time; id=10 AND SLEEP(0)-- returns instantly. The pattern replayed 3 times with consistent timing deltas vs baseline.","question":"What is the verdict for sqli?","candidates":{"vulnerable":"Time-based oracle is stable and matches baseline deltas, the payload reached the query engine","not_vulnerable":"A positive control proved the param reaches the query yet injection is parameterised","inconclusive":"The payload never reached the sink or no oracle confirmed the delay"},"target":"vulnerable"}
{"id":"ag2-ver-02","side":"offensive","category":"off_verdict","type":"choice","state":"The comment field reflects input into the page body. Payload <svg onload=alert(document.domain)> appears unencoded in the response, and browser_execute_js confirms the handler fired and alert ran in the page origin.","question":"What is the verdict for xss?","candidates":{"vulnerable":"The payload reached an executable HTML context and script ran in the page","not_vulnerable":"The input reflected but was entity-encoded and rendered inert","inconclusive":"The sink was never reached so execution could not be judged"},"target":"vulnerable"}
{"id":"ag2-ver-03","side":"offensive","category":"off_verdict","type":"choice","state":"The avatar_url parameter accepts a server-fetched URL. Injecting a unique Burp Collaborator subdomain produced both a DNS lookup and an HTTP GET from the target's egress IP, recorded in the interaction log.","question":"What is the verdict for ssrf?","candidates":{"vulnerable":"The server fetched the attacker URL and an out-of-band interaction confirmed it","not_vulnerable":"A control showed the param is fetched but external hosts are blocked at the resolver","inconclusive":"No callback oracle was available to observe whether the fetch happened"},"target":"vulnerable"}
{"id":"ag2-ver-04","side":"offensive","category":"off_verdict","type":"choice","state":"GET /api/profile?account_id=1004 returns the caller's own profile. Changing account_id to 1005 returns a different user's full JSON (distinct name, email, phone) with HTTP 200, confirmed against the baseline body of 1004.","question":"What is the verdict for idor?","candidates":{"vulnerable":"A changed object id returned another user's data with no authorization error","not_vulnerable":"A control changed the id but the server returned 403 or the caller's own record","inconclusive":"Only one account existed so cross-user access could not be tested"},"target":"vulnerable"}
{"id":"ag2-ver-05","side":"offensive","category":"off_verdict","type":"choice","state":"The sort parameter is numeric. Control: sort=1 and sort=2 return different, correctly ordered result sets, so the param drives the query. Payload sort=1 OR 1=1 returns the same body as sort=1, sort=1' returns an identical body with no error, and no boolean pair diverges.","question":"What is the verdict for sqli?","candidates":{"vulnerable":"A boolean or error payload changed the response in an injection-consistent way","not_vulnerable":"The param provably reaches the query yet all injection payloads are parameterised","inconclusive":"Payloads were blocked before reaching the query so validity is unproven"},"target":"not_vulnerable"}
{"id":"ag2-ver-06","side":"offensive","category":"off_verdict","type":"choice","state":"The name field is reflected on the confirmation page. Control: a unique marker string appears verbatim, so input reaches the sink. The payload <img src=x onerror=alert(1)> is returned HTML-entity-encoded as &lt;img...&gt; and the browser renders it as inert text with no DOM node created.","question":"What is the verdict for xss?","candidates":{"vulnerable":"The payload landed in an executable context and the handler fired","not_vulnerable":"The input provably reached the sink but is encoded and renders inert","inconclusive":"Reflection could not be located so the test was not valid"},"target":"not_vulnerable"}
{"id":"ag2-ver-07","side":"offensive","category":"off_verdict","type":"choice","state":"The return parameter sets a redirect. Control: return=/account issues a 302 to the same-origin path, so the param drives the Location header. return=https://evil.example and //evil.example are both rewritten to the site origin, and no external host appears in Location across variants.","question":"What is the verdict for open_redirect?","candidates":{"vulnerable":"The param sent the browser to an attacker-controlled external host","not_vulnerable":"The param provably drives the redirect but external hosts are normalised to same-origin","inconclusive":"No redirect occurred at all so the behaviour could not be judged"},"target":"not_vulnerable"}
{"id":"ag2-ver-08","side":"offensive","category":"off_verdict","type":"choice","state":"Every SQLi payload on the q parameter returns HTTP 403 with an identical WAF block page. Benign requests return 200 with results. No payload variant reached the application, so no baseline delta from the query engine was ever observed.","question":"What is the verdict for sqli?","candidates":{"vulnerable":"An injection payload produced a query-level anomaly versus baseline","not_vulnerable":"A payload reached the query and was provably parameterised","inconclusive":"A WAF blocked every payload so the sink was never exercised"},"target":"inconclusive"}
{"id":"ag2-ver-09","side":"offensive","category":"off_verdict","type":"choice","state":"The webhook_url parameter is suspected of blind SSRF. Payloads were injected, but the environment is Burp Community with no Collaborator, and the operator has not supplied an OOB callback domain. No response-timing difference is visible either.","question":"What is the verdict for ssrf?","candidates":{"vulnerable":"An out-of-band interaction confirmed the server fetched the attacker URL","not_vulnerable":"A control proved the fetch happens but egress is blocked","inconclusive":"No OOB oracle exists so a blind fetch cannot be observed"},"target":"inconclusive"}
{"id":"ag2-ver-10","side":"offensive","category":"off_verdict","type":"choice","state":"A stored-XSS payload was submitted in a profile bio. The bio only renders on a moderator approval screen that the test account cannot reach, and no second role is available. It is unknown whether the stored value is encoded on that screen.","question":"What is the verdict for stored_xss?","candidates":{"vulnerable":"The stored payload was observed executing in the rendering context","not_vulnerable":"The rendering page was reached and the stored value is encoded inert","inconclusive":"The rendering sink could not be reached so execution is unknown"},"target":"inconclusive"}
{"id":"ag2-chain-01","side":"offensive","category":"off_chain_worthy","type":"boolean","state":"An image-proxy parameter fetches arbitrary URLs. It reaches 169.254.169.254 and returns the raw instance metadata response, which includes temporary IAM credentials for the attached role.","question":"Is this worth escalating as a chain?","criteria":{"true":"It enables a concrete next step toward higher impact","false":"It is a standalone low with no realistic escalation path"},"target":true}
{"id":"ag2-chain-02","side":"offensive","category":"off_chain_worthy","type":"boolean","state":"The OAuth authorize endpoint accepts a redirect_uri whose host is not strictly validated. An attacker can register a redirect to their own domain and receive the victim's authorization code when the victim completes the flow.","question":"Is this worth escalating as a chain?","criteria":{"true":"It enables a concrete next step toward higher impact","false":"It is a standalone low with no realistic escalation path"},"target":true}
{"id":"ag2-chain-03","side":"offensive","category":"off_chain_worthy","type":"boolean","state":"A publicly readable JavaScript source map on the CDN includes the backend .env values, among them the HS256 JWT signing secret used to sign session tokens.","question":"Is this worth escalating as a chain?","criteria":{"true":"It enables a concrete next step toward higher impact","false":"It is a standalone low with no realistic escalation path"},"target":true}
{"id":"ag2-chain-04","side":"offensive","category":"off_chain_worthy","type":"boolean","state":"A search parameter reflects into a response header unescaped and allows CRLF injection. The attacker can inject a Set-Cookie header, fixing a known session identifier into the victim's browser before login.","question":"Is this worth escalating as a chain?","criteria":{"true":"It enables a concrete next step toward higher impact","false":"It is a standalone low with no realistic escalation path"},"target":true}
{"id":"ag2-chain-05","side":"offensive","category":"off_chain_worthy","type":"boolean","state":"A debug endpoint left enabled in production returns an internal service API key in its JSON output. The same key is accepted by the admin reporting API as a bearer token.","question":"Is this worth escalating as a chain?","criteria":{"true":"It enables a concrete next step toward higher impact","false":"It is a standalone low with no realistic escalation path"},"target":true}
{"id":"ag2-chain-06","side":"offensive","category":"off_chain_worthy","type":"boolean","state":"The API responds over HTTPS only and is HSTS-preloaded in browsers, but the HSTS header itself is missing on responses. No downgrade path or mixed content exists in the app.","question":"Is this worth escalating as a chain?","criteria":{"true":"It enables a concrete next step toward higher impact","false":"It is a standalone low with no realistic escalation path"},"target":false}
{"id":"ag2-chain-07","side":"offensive","category":"off_chain_worthy","type":"boolean","state":"The public 'About Us' page can be framed because frame-ancestors is unset. The page shows only static company text and has no buttons, forms, or authenticated actions.","question":"Is this worth escalating as a chain?","criteria":{"true":"It enables a concrete next step toward higher impact","false":"It is a standalone low with no realistic escalation path"},"target":false}
{"id":"ag2-chain-08","side":"offensive","category":"off_chain_worthy","type":"boolean","state":"The public signup form returns 'email already registered' for existing addresses and 'available' otherwise, allowing username enumeration. The product is a consumer app where registration is open and the behaviour is intended UX.","question":"Is this worth escalating as a chain?","criteria":{"true":"It enables a concrete next step toward higher impact","false":"It is a standalone low with no realistic escalation path"},"target":false}
{"id":"ag2-chain-09","side":"offensive","category":"off_chain_worthy","type":"boolean","state":"A developer helper reflects input into a page, but it only executes when the victim opens browser devtools and pastes the payload into the console themselves. No sink is reachable through normal navigation or a link.","question":"Is this worth escalating as a chain?","criteria":{"true":"It enables a concrete next step toward higher impact","false":"It is a standalone low with no realistic escalation path"},"target":false}
{"id":"ag2-chain-10","side":"offensive","category":"off_chain_worthy","type":"boolean","state":"A verbose 404 page prints the web framework name and version in its footer. No stack trace, path, token, or internal host is disclosed, and the version has no applicable public exploit at the running patch level.","question":"Is this worth escalating as a chain?","criteria":{"true":"It enables a concrete next step toward higher impact","false":"It is a standalone low with no realistic escalation path"},"target":false}
{"id":"ag3-001","side":"offensive","category":"off_test_class","type":"choice","state":"An image-preview endpoint fetches any user-supplied URL server-side and returns the body; it reaches internal 169.254.169.254.","question":"Highest-value test class here?","candidates":{"ssrf":"Coerce the server to request internal hosts and cloud metadata","mixed_content":"Page loads an http asset over https","hsts":"Strict-Transport-Security header missing"},"target":"ssrf"}
{"id":"ag3-002","side":"offensive","category":"off_test_class","type":"choice","state":"A SOAP endpoint parses user XML with a parser that resolves external entities and echoes node content in the response.","question":"Highest-value test class here?","candidates":{"xxe":"Declare an external entity to read local files and reach internal hosts","cookie_flags":"Session cookie lacks HttpOnly","referrer_policy":"Referrer-Policy header not set"},"target":"xxe"}
{"id":"ag3-003","side":"offensive","category":"off_test_class","type":"choice","state":"GET /api/invoices/{id} returns full invoice data; changing id to a neighbouring value returns another tenant's invoice with no authorization check.","question":"Highest-value test class here?","candidates":{"idor":"Access other users' objects by changing a direct object reference","clickjacking":"Page is framable without X-Frame-Options","hsts":"HSTS not enforced on the API host"},"target":"idor"}
{"id":"ag3-004","side":"offensive","category":"off_test_class","type":"choice","state":"A standard user sends POST /api/admin/users/create; the server executes it and creates an admin, exposing an admin-only function to a low-privilege role.","question":"Highest-value test class here?","candidates":{"bfla":"Invoke an admin-only function as a lower-privilege user","cookie_flags":"Cookie missing Secure flag","mixed_content":"Mixed http and https resources on the admin page"},"target":"bfla"}
{"id":"ag3-005","side":"offensive","category":"off_test_class","type":"choice","state":"A product search parameter is concatenated into a SQL query; a single quote returns a database syntax error and a boolean pair yields different row counts.","question":"Highest-value test class here?","candidates":{"sqli":"Inject SQL to read database contents via boolean/union/error channels","referrer_policy":"Missing Referrer-Policy on the search page","hsts":"No HSTS header on responses"},"target":"sqli"}
{"id":"ag3-006","side":"offensive","category":"off_test_class","type":"choice","state":"A greeting field is rendered into a server-side Jinja2 template; the payload {{7*7}} returns 49 in the response body.","question":"Highest-value test class here?","candidates":{"ssti":"Reach template evaluation for data read and potential RCE","clickjacking":"Greeting page can be framed","cookie_flags":"Session cookie lacks SameSite"},"target":"ssti"}
{"id":"ag3-007","side":"offensive","category":"off_test_class","type":"choice","state":"The registration endpoint binds the whole JSON body to the user model; adding \"role\":\"admin\" to the payload persists and grants admin.","question":"Highest-value test class here?","candidates":{"mass_assignment":"Set unexposed privileged fields by adding them to the request body","cookie_flags":"Cookie lacks HttpOnly after signup","hsts":"Signup response omits HSTS"},"target":"mass_assignment"}
{"id":"ag3-008","side":"offensive","category":"off_test_class","type":"choice","state":"A one-time coupon applies a balance credit; the check-then-write has no lock, so parallel redemptions of the same coupon each credit the account.","question":"Highest-value test class here?","candidates":{"race_condition":"Fire concurrent requests to double-redeem past the single-use limit","mixed_content":"Coupon page serves an http script","referrer_policy":"No Referrer-Policy on the coupon flow"},"target":"race_condition"}
{"id":"ag3-009","side":"offensive","category":"off_test_class","type":"choice","state":"The OAuth authorize endpoint reflects redirect_uri without allowlist validation and redirects to any attacker-controlled host, carrying the authorization code.","question":"Highest-value test class here?","candidates":{"oauth_redirect_hijack":"Steal the auth code/token by pointing redirect_uri at an attacker host","clickjacking":"Consent screen is framable","hsts":"Authorization host missing HSTS"},"target":"oauth_redirect_hijack"}
{"id":"ag3-010","side":"offensive","category":"off_test_class","type":"choice","state":"The API accepts a JWT with alg switched from RS256 to HS256, verifying the signature with the public key as the HMAC secret.","question":"Highest-value test class here?","candidates":{"jwt_alg_confusion":"Forge a valid token by abusing algorithm confusion with the public key","cookie_flags":"JWT stored in a cookie without Secure","referrer_policy":"Token-bearing page lacks Referrer-Policy"},"target":"jwt_alg_confusion"}
{"id":"ag3-015","side":"offensive","category":"off_scanner_adjudication","type":"boolean","state":"A scanner flagged /.env; fetching it returns a readable file with DB_PASSWORD and a live AWS secret key that authenticate successfully.","question":"Is this a real, reportable finding?","criteria":{"true":"confirmed impact","false":"noise"},"target":true}
{"id":"ag3-016","side":"offensive","category":"off_scanner_adjudication","type":"boolean","state":"A scanner flagged an exposed /.git/ directory; dumping it with git-dumper recovers application source and a committed API token that is still valid.","question":"Is this a real, reportable finding?","criteria":{"true":"confirmed impact","false":"noise"},"target":true}
{"id":"ag3-017","side":"offensive","category":"off_scanner_adjudication","type":"boolean","state":"A scanner flagged Spring Boot /actuator/heapdump; downloading it and parsing the heap yields live session tokens and a plaintext datasource password.","question":"Is this a real, reportable finding?","criteria":{"true":"confirmed impact","false":"noise"},"target":true}
{"id":"ag3-018","side":"offensive","category":"off_scanner_adjudication","type":"boolean","state":"A scanner flagged an exposed admin console; it loads without authentication and its script-console runs OS commands, returning the output of id.","question":"Is this a real, reportable finding?","criteria":{"true":"confirmed impact","false":"noise"},"target":true}
{"id":"ag3-019","side":"offensive","category":"off_scanner_adjudication","type":"boolean","state":"A scanner flagged an open Elasticsearch on 9200; GET /_search with no auth returns customer records including names and emails.","question":"Is this a real, reportable finding?","criteria":{"true":"confirmed impact","false":"noise"},"target":true}
{"id":"ag3-020","side":"offensive","category":"off_scanner_adjudication","type":"boolean","state":"A scanner flagged a missing X-Frame-Options header on a static marketing page; the page has no authenticated state and no state-changing action.","question":"Is this a real, reportable finding?","criteria":{"true":"confirmed impact","false":"noise"},"target":false}
{"id":"ag3-021","side":"offensive","category":"off_scanner_adjudication","type":"boolean","state":"A scanner flagged a Server: nginx/1.18.0 version banner; the version is disclosed but no corresponding exploit or further access follows from it.","question":"Is this a real, reportable finding?","criteria":{"true":"confirmed impact","false":"noise"},"target":false}
{"id":"ag3-022","side":"offensive","category":"off_scanner_adjudication","type":"boolean","state":"A scanner flagged that OPTIONS and TRACE are enabled; TRACE only echoes the request and no cross-site or header-injection impact is demonstrable.","question":"Is this a real, reportable finding?","criteria":{"true":"confirmed impact","false":"noise"},"target":false}
